<title>USA: Britton &amp; Koontz says may set stock split.</title>
<headline>Britton &amp; Koontz says may set stock split.</headline>
<dateline>NATCHEZ, Miss. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britton &amp; Koontz Capital Corp said Tuesday that its board of directors has proposed a four-for-one stock split provided an increase in shares to 12 million is approved at its annual shareholders meeting later this year.</p>
<p>The company currently has about three million shares authorized. The shareholders meeting is to be held in March or April, it said.</p>
<p>Britton &amp; Koontz Capital is the parent company of Britton &amp; Koontz First National Bank.</p>
</text>
